In Section~\ref{sec-twist}, we prove that $\gZ(\wg^\vth,[0])$ is always Poisson-commutative and that it has an algebraically independent infinite set of generators, see  Corollary~\ref{cl-red} and Theorem~\ref{twist-inf}. 
This shows that unlike the case of the trivial $\vth$, there is a major difference between  
$\gZ(\wg^\vth,t^{-1})$ and $\gZ(\wg^\vth,[0])$. 

In Section~\ref{Q}, we consider images of  $\gZ(\wg^\vth,t)$  and $\gZ(\wg^\vth,[0])$ in 
$\gS((\wg^\vth/(t^m-1))\cong\gS(\g)$. We show that the image of  $\gZ(\wg^\vth,[0])$ is generated by 
