For $\alpha>0$ and $\beta>1$, the first term of the right side of Eq. (\ref{Dbtbm1Eabg}) results to be
\begin{eqnarray}
&&\hspace{-1em}\int_0^t \left(\ln \left(t-t_1\right)\right)
t_1^{\beta-2}E^{\gamma}_{\alpha,\beta-1}\left(\lambda t_1^{\alpha}\right)dt_1\nonumber \\ &&\hspace{-1em}=
t^{\beta-1}\left(\ln t-\gamma_0\right)
\left(
\left(\beta-1\right)E^{\gamma}_{\alpha,\beta-1}\left(\lambda t^{\alpha}\right)  %\right.\nonumber \\ &&\hspace{-1em}\left.
