As shown in Fig.~\ref{reward_curve}, the convergence performance of the proposed STTD algorithm is evaluated. The envelope area is formulated based on the average reward calculated over every four steps and the corresponding variance. The results show that the reward gradually increases, undergoes minor fluctuations, and ultimately stabilizes around $4.3$. Notably, a temporary decrease in the average reward to $3.2$ is observed at approximately episode $150$, primarily due to extensive explorations. These explorations result in several users' sensing and resource constraints being violated, thereby leading to degraded QoE performance. Overall, the proposed STTD algorithm demonstrates the ability to converge to a high and stable reward, which demonstrates its effectiveness.


\subsection{QoE Probability Distribution}
\begin{figure}[!t]
