\begin{Remark}[Key Properties of \(S^N\)] \label{remark:sn}
The alternating cycle function exhibits three fundamental properties:
\begin{enumerate}
\item \textbf{Periodicity}: \(S^N\) has a period of \(2N\), i.e., \(S^N(k + 2N) = S^N(k)\) for all \(k \in \mathbb{N}\).
\item \textbf{Wave Pattern}: Over each interval of length \(2N\), \(S^N(k)\) decreases from \(N\) to \(1\) and then increases from \(1\) to \(N\).
\item \textbf{Local Palindromy}: Within each \(2N\)-length block, the sequence is palindromic (symmetric under reversal).
\end{enumerate}
\end{Remark}

