The explicit formula for \(1\)-\(\operatorname{CUT}(n)\) vertices reveals a fractal structure governed by the alternating cycle function \(S^N(k)\). We now extend this result to the original \(\operatorname{CUT}(n)\) polytope using the probabilistic duality established in Section~3.1.

\begin{Corollary}[Encoded Vertices of \(\operatorname{CUT}(n)\)]
For \(n \geq 3\), the encoded vertices \(w^n(k)\) of \(\operatorname{CUT}(n)\) are given by:
\[
w^n(k) = 2^{\binom{n}{2}} - 1 - \left[ 2^{\binom{n-1}{2}} (k - 1) + \sum_{j=1}^{n-2} 2^{\binom{j}{2}} \left( S^{2^j}(k) - 1 \right) \right].
\]
\end{Corollary}
\begin{proof}
This follows directly from the duality \(\operatorname{CUT}(n) = \mathbf{1} - (1\)-\(\operatorname{CUT}(n))\) and the encoding map \(\code(\cdot)\).
\end{proof}
