The build-up of bias at low $\xmax$ is due to the parabola fitting procedure in the $\xmax$ reconstruction method.
Since the reconstruction method involves limited sampling, the parabola fit becomes biased with no equal number of simulations on either side of the parabola, leading to a bias in lower $\xmax$.

