We also study the variation of the bias and resolution of the $\xmax$ reconstruction procedure with respect to varying $\xmax$ in \Cref{fig:bias-resolution}. 
But apart from expected bias at low $\xmax$, we can see that both the bias and resolution for the simulations are similar between neural network predictions and per-event CoREAS simulations, making neural networks a viable simulation tool for simulating radio pulses.
