The preliminary IceCat-2 catalog includes 365 track-like alerts, with their sky distribution shown in Fig.~\ref{fig:skymap}. Issued at an average rate of 26.8 events per year, $\sim$9.9 and 17 fall into the Gold and Bronze channels, corresponding to average astrophysical probabilities of 50\% and 30\%, assuming a power-law spectrum with index 2.19. This selection, adopted in IceCat-1 and currently used in real-time alerts, is based on an earlier IceCube measurement. Future versions of the catalog will incorporate an updated spectral index value, reflecting the softer spectrum observed in muon track events by IceCube. The impact of this change will be investigated in forthcoming studies.

