\vspace{-4mm}
\section{Summary}
\label{sec:summary}
\vspace{-3mm}
To enhance multi-messenger capabilities, IceCube has developed an improved reconstruction method for its real-time alert system. As a result, the original IceCube Event Catalog of Alert Tracks (IceCat-1) has been revised. IceCat-2 incorporates the new reconstructions, updated calibrations, exclusion of likely CR-induced events, and new alerts since the last release. We present the preliminary IceCat-2 catalog, which contains 365 track-like alerts from May 2011 (IC-110514A) to January 2, 2025 (IC-250102A). Studies of spatial correlations with astrophysical sources will take advantage of IceCat-2 significantly (e.g., ~\cite{new_tdes_searches}). Notably, it improves the angular uncertainty areas by a factor $\sim5$, with median 50\% and 90\% containment areas of 0.4 and 1.3 square degrees, respectively. A public release of the full catalog will follow a peer-reviewed publication, alongside several analyses on source population correlations.

