The results are highly encouraging: QRGMM$^\dagger$’s approximations consistently track the true values across all measures, demonstrating robust accuracy. Conversely, CWGAN exhibits notable discrepancies, especially in \( r_2(l) \) and \( r_3(l) \), reflecting weaker performance. This comparison underscores QRGMM’s superior capability in capturing complex risk measures, QRGMM’s reliability significantly outshines CWGAN, demonstrating its applicability in SCF credit risk management. Notably, these figures vividly offer a clear, immediate view of how risk measures evolve with loan amount \( l \), providing decision-makers with an intuitive tool for understanding the risk dynamics, thereby greatly facilitating loan sizing decisions.







\subsection{Real-World Data Experiments}\label{sec:real}

\subsubsection{Big Mart Sales Dataset}\label{sec:bigmart}

