\subsubsection{Amazon CBEC Dataset}\label{sec:amazon}

To further assess the effectiveness of QRGMM$^\dagger$ in a real-world cross-border e-commerce (CBEC) context, we also conduct experiments on a dataset from a company conducting China-to-U.S. CBEC on Amazon. This dataset includes 3,495 sales records from the first quarter of 2023, covering 99 product categories across 131 stores. The products are managed by 23 distinct product selection teams and 23 sales teams, forming various team pairings. As noted earlier, these pairings exhibit combinatorial effects due to differences in team capability and cross-team collaboration. The dataset also features seven continuous variables: advertising expenses, clicks, impressions, sale price, product cost, average rating, and number of reviews. Again, we randomly split the data into training and test subsets with a 4:1 ratio across 100 replications. And we set \( m = 60 \).


