One must also consider how well does the $FoM$ represent the performance of the tuner. The usual definition of the $FoM$ describes the performance of the tuner as a single, average number, as seen for example in Eq.\,\ref{eq:fom}. For a cavity with a tuner, where the RF power amplifier  requirement is determined  by the highest power dissipation in the tuner, this average indicator is not appropriate. Looking at Figure\,\ref{fig:qfrtvsep}, we see $Q_{FRT}$ plotted as a function of the permittivity for the cases of the 50\,Hz and 104\,Hz tuning range. This information is necessary to specify the power rating of the RF amplifier driving the cavity. The amplifier must be able to address the requirement at the lowest value of $Q_{FRT}$, otherwise the cavity voltage would not be maintained at all values of the detuning. It is obvious that this condition is specified by the value of $Q_{FRT}$ at the lowest permittivity.

