%\\ &
=-\varkappa^{4}\frac{\pi}{2}\lt[\frac{2}{\beta}+\lt(1-\frac{1}{\beta^{2}}\rt)\ln\lt(\frac{1+\beta}{1-\beta}\rt)\rt]\!(t^r).
%\end{split}
\end{align}
 The next term is for $k=1$. 
 Evaluating ${\color{red}\aV}\cdot \nh= {\color{red}a}\cos\theta $, $\qV\cdot \nh= q\cos\theta $ and $\qV\cdot {\color{red}\aV}=aq$ 
(where ${\color{red}a}$ and $q$ are tacitly functions of $t^{r}$)
