\begin{abstract}
It has been shown recently that optimal control problems with the dynamical constraint given by second order system admit a regular Lagrangian formulation. This implies that the optimality conditions can be obtained in a new form based on the variational approach. In this paper we extend the necessary optimality conditions obtained in  \cite{sato2025} to second order optimality conditions and discuss the role of the new Lagrangian.
\end{abstract}
